skill: "litigation-regulatory-risk-scanner"
sections[3]:
  - "# litigation-regulatory-risk-scanner\n\nScan the company's exposure surface: demand letters, regulatory inquiries, incident aftermath and deal diligence. Classifies exposure, scores severity, starts the response clock with the right template, and instantiates the M&A legal audit checklist when a deal flag is set. Use on any legal threat, inquiry or deal signal.\n\nOwner: role-general-counsel (pod-gna, legal). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - search_web\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"trigger documents (demand letter, regulator letter, incident report, deal flag); contracts and policies via register; jurisdiction registry; M&A checklist template ma-audit-template.toon\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/legal/risk-register.toon with exposure[], severity score, response clock and owner; inquiry-response.toon skeleton; ma-audit-checklist.toon when triggered\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Log the trigger with its received date; the response clock starts at receipt and every computed deadline in this run derives from that date, never from the processing date.\n2. Classify the exposure: contract dispute, tort claim, statutory claim, regulatory inquiry, government investigation; the class decides the template and the escalation path.\n3. Score severity on the policy scale (financial range, operational disruption, precedent risk, deadline pressure); a severity score without its factor breakdown is rewritten.\n4. For regulatory inquiries, build the response skeleton from the template: acknowledgement path, document hold notice, production log format and the deadline clock with calendar dates.\n5. Issue the document hold notice content when litigation or investigation is plausible; the hold covers the custodians and systems the trigger names, and lists them.\n6. When a deal flag is set, instantiate ma-audit-checklist.toon: corporate records, IP chain of title, key contracts change-of-control, employment, privacy compliance and litigation history sections with owner per item.\n7. Emit ask_question for anything above the escalation threshold (external counsel engagement, insurer notice, disclosure decisions); this skill prepares the record, it does not make the call.\n8. Write risk-register.toon and update it as items resolve; the quarterly review reads this register, and items without a next-review date are treated as open.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nhold notices and clocks recorded; deal checklist to deal team; escalations to operator.\n"
